nes-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T19:12:36-08:00","id":26213,"title":"","content":"Of course! Though my conversion is still very much in the theoretical stages, so it will be some time before it hits the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T21:54:06-08:00","id":26300,"title":"","content":"Sounds good! I'm always interested in seeing more of things like these. I've been trying to build a pretty comprehensive rule set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T21:55:45-08:00","id":26990,"title":"","content":"Excellent translation of the curses to the new system! I'd really like to use these in a conversion I plan on doing for my next game (after my current WoD game is over). I think your tying the curse to the individual Kindred's humanity is awesome. As the Man weakens, the Curse becomes stronger and more restrictive.<br /> <br /> Question about the Giovanni curse though: As written, you have their victims having to succeed on a roll that is limited by their attacker's Humanity. Wouldn't this become harder to succeed at (for the victim) the more inhumane the Kindred becomes? Maybe it should be <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Vessels must succeed on a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll, limited by <b>10 minus the Necromancer\u2019s Humanity</b>, not to scream or struggle</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">.</span> </div> </div> </div> I think that would bring it in line with the other curses that get more restrictive as their humanity wanes.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni are known to feast on the dead and the dying in classic WoD, due to the extra damage that their Kiss inflicted on their victims. Perhaps another curse option for them would be that along with the usual one point of lethal damage inflicted for every Vitae taken, the Necromancer inflicts another 8 - Humanity points of bashing damage as well. This way, some of the old flavor is retained and it also keeps in line with the linking of all the curses to Humanity. Just my two cents.<br /> <br /> This really is great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T00:04:50-08:00","id":27037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=26990#post26990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent translation of the curses to the new system! I'd really like to use these in a conversion I plan on doing for my next game (after my current WoD game is over). I think your tying the curse to the individual Kindred's humanity is awesome. As the Man weakens, the Curse becomes stronger and more restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I appreciate it! I can't take credit for tying the Humanity factor in, as that's the new design aesthetic for the updated Requiem core! But I liked that so much, and I've run enough &quot;Masquiem&quot; chronicles, that I wanted to have these jive with the new material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=26990#post26990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Giovanni curse though: As written, you have their victims having to succeed on a roll that is limited by their attacker's Humanity. Wouldn't this become harder to succeed at (for the victim) the more inhumane the Kindred becomes? Maybe it should be I think that would bring it in line with the other curses that get more restrictive as their humanity wanes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the Giovanni: My intention was that the more inhumane the Necromancer becomes, the more difficult it becomes for her to feed on the fly, or in a convenient way at all. A Humanity 2 Giovanni's victim will rarely succeed in not screaming, since he'd only have 2 dice to resist the urge, even if he were willing to be fed from. The vampire's not likely to grab someone off the street if the guy might scream...unless she beats him into unconsciousness. Even then, the marks are still going to be a problem...<br /> <br /> If it's 10 - Humanity, it means it gets <i>easier </i>to feed as the vampire's Humanity gets lower. That said, I ought to add a duration on how long the bite marks last.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I think just realised what the confusion was. By limited, I mean the roll is &quot;capped&quot;, not subtracted. i.e., Bob the Blood Doll has Resolve + Composure 5, but Lucretia the Giovanni has Humanity 3, so he only gets 3 dice to resist. If her Humanity were 5 or higher, he'd get his full pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=26990#post26990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni are known to feast on the dead and the dying in classic WoD, due to the extra damage that their Kiss inflicted on their victims. Perhaps another curse option for them would be that along with the usual one point of lethal damage inflicted for every Vitae taken, the Necromancer inflicts another 8 - Humanity points of bashing damage as well. This way, some of the old flavor is retained and it also keeps in line with the linking of all the curses to Humanity. Just my two cents.<br /> <br /> This really is great work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I decided not to add the damage factor because I preferred it as a Masquerade breachy weakness, rather than a deadly one. You could easily build the Bane that way, though. This is just my take on it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-10-2013, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T03:20:18-08:00","id":27098,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see what you meant now. Funny how you can read something one way, then hear it explained, then read it again and get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1257,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","user":"Kerensky","date":". 12-10-2013, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:25:01-08:00","id":27336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=27098#post27098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see what you meant now. Funny how you can read something one way, then hear it explained, then read it again and get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I've made the same kind of mistake. I use &quot;limited&quot; because that's what they tend to use in the official lingo of late, but I prefer capped, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T17:01:46-08:00","id":29010,"title":"","content":"Setites have been updated (the old version was pretty superfluous in certain contexts); still trying to think up something better for Nosferatu that isn't merely a reskin of what's going in Blood &amp; Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:56:03-08:00","id":29182,"title":"","content":"I think you did a good job making it more succinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T01:10:00-08:00","id":29197,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I realised that the other version probably had too good a chance of being a kill switch on a lucky roll, and I wanted it to be more of a behavior affecting weakness. Plus, it basically meant nothing at high Blood Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T03:19:37-08:00","id":29227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=29010#post29010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]still trying to think up something better for Nosferatu that isn't merely a reskin of what's going in Blood &amp; Smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using Social Influence rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T03:45:17-08:00","id":29232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=29227#post29227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you using Social Influence rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of that, but I wasn't sure how to configure it. I had the idea that they had to get through a number of extra Doors equal to 10 - Humanity, but it doesn't make that much sense in the context of just being monstrous. Since I want to be true to the spirit of the original, I at least have to keep the ugliness aspect. Admittedly, I've only ever used the new Nos weakness when running hybrid games, so I've not had that much experience in testing this version.<br /> <br /> Right now, I like the flavour of what I've got written down, in that they become more monstrous as they fall to the Beast. But I feel like the social penalties I've created are a bit redundant, given that by the time you hit the point where the bane really hurts, you're already dealing with some pretty nasty Social penalties from low Humanity. Obfuscate also complicates the issue, since it doesn't make sense to apply the penalty when you're using Familiar Stranger, unless you're going with the Requiem style aura-of-creepiness weakness, which I'm trying not to do.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm over-thinking it? Maybe this needs to be a soft roleplay kind of weakness. You get monstrous as you fall to the Beast. That's it. There are lots of consequences for being a monster walking about in public. Food for thought...I don't know that I'll go that route, but it gets my brain ticking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-13-2013, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T07:39:31-08:00","id":29299,"title":"","content":"The aditional Doors thing is an option. Another one that I sugested back when the Nos Bane was still in development and I think gives interesting hooks is this: When interacting with mortals whose Integrity (or similar) rating is higher than her Humanity the default First Impresion is one step lower than usual (so normally Hostile).<br /> <br /> This forces Nos that want to have meanigful interactions to seek jaged and broken individuals (or use their own Nightmare powers to bring prospective people down to that level).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T07:53:19-08:00","id":29305,"title":"","content":"I was going to suggest something similar to Thorbes, but I was going to say since the Masquerade weakness was not even having an appearance attribute at all, having them auto-fail appearance based social rolls against anyone with higher humanity/splat equivalent. But I like the lowered first impression idea better. Has the same feel, but doesn't need to differentiate between which social rolls are &quot;appearance based&quot;. They just make a poor first impression because they're ugly, except on those who are too broken to care. It's also still a pretty hefty weakness without totally crippling social Nos character concepts, and I like that it piggybacks on an existing system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T13:31:57-08:00","id":29496,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think Impressions is the right direction, and the flavour of it is that they get Masquerade breachy as they get lower Humanity. Thanks Thorbes &amp; co.! I'll got back to the lab and see what I can come up with. I have to account for Obfuscate, but I like the idea that you're so frigging hideous that it even comes through your magic powers--that aspect skirts VERY closely to being too much like the proper Requiem Nos weakness, but I can deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:42:37-08:00","id":29538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=29496#post29496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think Impressions is the right direction, and the flavour of it is that they get Masquerade breachy as they get lower Humanity. Thanks Thorbes &amp; co.! I'll got back to the lab and see what I can come up with. I have to account for Obfuscate, but I like the idea that you're so frigging hideous that it even comes through your magic powers--that aspect skirts VERY closely to being too much like the proper Requiem Nos weakness, but I can deal.</div> </div> </div> </div> How did Masquerade handle obfuscate vs. the Nos weakness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T16:09:01-08:00","id":29592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=29538#post29538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How did Masquerade handle obfuscate vs. the Nos weakness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that the Nosferatu weakness possed any problem for obfuscate back in Masquerade. The Nos weakness back then was that you had an appearance of 0. Back then, appearance was another attribute like strength (the list of attributes were different then). So while the worst looking human might have an appearance of 1, a Nos had 0, so they looked worse than any human. Appearance played a role in first impressions, so most people would react poorly on a first encounter. Anyways, obfuscate makes you psychically invisible so appearance wouldn't matter unless someone could pierce the illusion (or you revealed yourself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T20:21:20-08:00","id":29684,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate in Masquerade didn't so much negate the weakness so much as make Nosferatu playable at all. It was still a bit of a cheat, but, honestly, the Nosferatu needed all the help they could get. Plus I think it required a lot of effort to create a persona with an effective &quot;Appearance&quot; trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T20:59:15-08:00","id":29699,"title":"","content":"Eh, seems to me like it wouldn't be necessary to make special provision for the interaction between the Nos weakness and Obfuscate, then. Or you could allow Obfuscate and other supernatural disguise powers to &quot;cover up&quot; the weakness, but apply a humanity cap or a (10 - humanity) penalty on rolls to activate such powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T01:13:16-08:00","id":29803,"title":"","content":"Nos Bane has been updated! I went with something like Thorbes' idea, which fit well when I remembered that's what the flavour text of the V20 Dark Ages weakness says it ought to do. I also decided not to specify that they're &quot;ugly&quot;, because I think that word raises too many issues. Rather, they're &quot;physically monstrous&quot;. Storytellers and players can decide what that means, whether it's that they're grotesque, or frightening, or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-14-2013, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:50:45-08:00","id":32730,"title":"","content":"Big update, now that Blood and Smoke is out! As I go through B&amp;S, I'll make any appropriate changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T00:54:42-08:00","id":68288,"title":"","content":"These are still excellent. Even if you don'tr want to use full clans, they make good Bloodline banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:16:17-08:00","id":68611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=68288#post68288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are still excellent. Even if you don'tr want to use full clans, they make good Bloodline banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm more or less happy with all the main clans, unless someone can point out any unintended consequences that I've missed (or something better). I'm still not sold on Caitiff, though; it's a bit over complicated, and it probably doesn't need the Humanity factor--I've always assumed the draw of playing a Caitiff was being <i>free </i>of a Clan Curse, at the cost of having fewer Discipline advantages. I feel like Revenants in Blood and Smoke are much more interesting than what I came up with, and if you want Caitiff, you ought to just use those guys and rebrand slightly. I'm pretty sure Caitiff is even a term in Requiem...it turns up in the core, then never again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:31:37-08:00","id":68618,"title":"","content":"I never noticed that. It is in the core, only on page 86.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> caitiff: A vampire of unknown clan. Usage: Am I to under-<br /> stand that this caitiff is truly a Nosferatu of Wellington\u2019s brood?<br /> How could I not have guessed? </div> </div> </div>A holdover from Masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T19:18:16-08:00","id":68762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=68618#post68618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never noticed that. It is in the core, only on page 86.<br /> <br /> A holdover from Masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so? I guess they liked that term (in a different context), but then thought better of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:23:47-07:00","id":233757,"title":"","content":"Thread necromancy!<br /> <br /> Been a while since I looked at this, and after playing the new edition for a while, I've made some revisions. Mostly it's wording, and removing unnecessary restrictions. The Lasombra Bane is wholly different, so tell me what y'all think. I've also rearranged the document a bit so that Conditions are listed on the last page.<br /> <br /> <b>Question: </b>I'm still not very satisfied with the Tremere Bane. The second step bond with the first drink part is fine, but I feel like the part that scales with Humanity is a lot of dice rolling to keep up with, and it doesn't add a lot of flavour. I'm okay with leaving it as is, but does anyone have a better idea?<br /> <br /> For ease of access:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35TjBITm90RVZwck0/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35TjBITm90RVZwck0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35TjBITm90RVZwck0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35TjBITm90RVZwck0/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (I'm just gonna drop the Scribd link since it does bizarre things to the PDF, and their system isn't conducive to sharing)<br /> <br /> Will update the OP.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:11:54-07:00","id":233839,"title":"","content":"How about this for the Tremere: Tremere are more susceptible to the blood bond. Whenever she drinks another Kindred's vitae, she must make a humanity roll. Success on the roll creates a blood bond at the first level. Failure indicates that the bond starts at the second stage. No Tremere may attempt to completely resist the formation of a bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:13:20-07:00","id":233840,"title":"","content":"Well, the Venrue Bane and the Mekhet Bane show that not every Clan Bane has to relate directly to the character's Humanity <i>value</i>, as long as it relates to Humanity and generally gets worse as Humanity drops. So what if Tremere can't apply their Touchstone bonus to Breaking Point rolls for causing direct harm to their regnants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:37:54-07:00","id":233876,"title":"","content":"@Charlaquin: I really like that! I might just add that in. Lemme give it a think, and see if anyone else has cool ideas...<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>So, something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Yielding Curse):</b> Tremere are easily controlled through blood bonds. A Warlock will form a second step Vinculum the first time she drinks from a vampire. If a bond takes hold, the Tremere may not apply her Touchstone bonus on detachment rolls incurred for acting against her regnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-19-2014, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:01:32-07:00","id":233888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233876#post233876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin: I really like that! I might just add that in. Lemme give it a think, and see if anyone else has cool ideas...<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>So, something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Yielding Curse):</b> Tremere are easily controlled through blood bonds. A Warlock will form a second step Vinculum the first time she drinks from a vampire. If a bond takes hold, the Tremere may not apply her Touchstone bonus on detachment rolls incurred for acting against her regnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that make the curse pretty much ineffective after a Kindred reached Humanity 5 if they only have 1 Touchstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:02:25-07:00","id":233889,"title":"","content":"Damn, good to see this still going! I may have use for this in the near future. Still working on the Salubri Healers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:13:11-07:00","id":233895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233888#post233888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wouldn't that make the curse pretty much ineffective after a Kindred reached Humanity 5 if they only have 1 Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair point, but I figure if a character doesn't regain or find more Touchstones at that point, she's got bigger problems than her Bane. That said, I'm not 100% on it, and I liked your idea, too. If using Touchstones is too esoteric, maybe it could be as simple as &quot;Roll the Tremere's Humanity after a first step blood bond takes; on failure, it progresses to the second step.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:16:05-07:00","id":233900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233889#post233889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, good to see this still going! I may have use for this in the near future. Still working on the Salubri Healers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've unfortunately let the Healers slide a bit! But they're on my to do list once my summer pile of stuff gets cleared up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:28:41-07:00","id":233910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233900#post233900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've unfortunately let the Healers slide a bit! But they're on my to do list once my summer pile of stuff gets cleared up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A bit unfortunate, but quite alright! I'd love to see what you do. If ya need any input, I am always free. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In any case, hope your work load goes well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:44:03-07:00","id":233915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233910#post233910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A bit unfortunate, but quite alright! I'd love to see what you do. If ya need any input, I am always free. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In any case, hope your work load goes well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been probably one of the most creative summers I've ever had, so it's going super well. Exhausting though. And it's not done yet, but the finishing line is starting to become visible.<br /> <br /> I'll keep you up to date on the Salubri! And I have a whole backlog of other Vampire and Demon stuff I should post here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:52:13-07:00","id":233917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233888#post233888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't that make the curse pretty much ineffective after a Kindred reached Humanity 5 if they only have 1 Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that specific aspect of the Bane, but there's still the straight-to-stage-2 part. Besides, isn't the Ventrue Bane (The Requiem one) also pretty much ineffective after they reach Humanity 5?<br /> <br /> Alternative idea: Normally, you can only be bound to one regnant, right? What if you drop the straight-to-stage-2 part and instead say that the Tremere can be bound to (8-Humanity) regnants at once, to a minimum of 1. Write the name of any regnants beyond the first on the line next to the highest available Humanity dot starting with 6, and if you regain Humanity they get detached like Touchstones, but return if you lose Humanity again. Gives a great reason for the Tremere tradition of bonding neonates to high-ranking Warlocks - you want to make sure those bonds are taken up by people with the Clan's interests in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:54:57-07:00","id":234327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=233917#post233917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only that specific aspect of the Bane, but there's still the straight-to-stage-2 part. Besides, isn't the Ventrue Bane (The Requiem one) also pretty much ineffective after they reach Humanity 5?<br /> <br /> Alternative idea: Normally, you can only be bound to one regnant, right? What if you drop the straight-to-stage-2 part and instead say that the Tremere can be bound to (8-Humanity) regnants at once, to a minimum of 1. Write the name of any regnants beyond the first on the line next to the highest available Humanity dot starting with 6, and if you regain Humanity they get detached like Touchstones, but return if you lose Humanity again. Gives a great reason for the Tremere tradition of bonding neonates to high-ranking Warlocks - you want to make sure those bonds are taken up by people with the Clan's interests in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that in concept, but I think it might be too much book keeping. I should have an extra document of...extras.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna change it to Charlaquin's Touchstone idea, but I'm still open to suggestions, especially if that can be tweaked further.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T16:32:27-07:00","id":280249,"title":"","content":"This is terrific. Do more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:30:06-07:00","id":280478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=280249#post280249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is terrific. Do more!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I keep meaning to do more! And I will soon. A lot of it comes down to how willing I am to translate the old disciplines that aren't in the Translation Guide, and HOW I should do it. But I have a WIP for some of the other Clans, and I'll get around to posting them soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:53:54-07:00","id":280531,"title":"","content":"Always love to see your work. Love the 13 Licks, but you know that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:20:22-07:00","id":281513,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's go deeper down the rabbit hole:<br /> <br /> <b>Daughters of Cacophony</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Sirens, Maenads<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Majesty, Melpominee, Resilience<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Discordant Curse): </b>Daughters of Cacophony constantly, <i>maddeningly</i>, hear music running through their heads. Driven to distraction, a Siren's dice pools are limited by her Humanity when making Perception rolls, or when trying to recall or memorize information (<b>World of Darkness Rulebook</b>, p. 44). Treat any failures as dramatic failures.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Manipulation or Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Melpominee </b>is easy enough to just translate into NWoD rules. Fiddle with some numbers, determine dice pools, throw in some Conditions, etc. You can probably do this on your own. The thing is, it's...a strange discipline. Truth be told (YMMV), it's not even very good. It's a hodgepodge of abilities better represented with Majesty, Nightmare, or Dominate (or devotions of those powers), and the last tier is just &quot;Two for the price of one!&quot; All this is fine in <b>Masquerade</b>, where a bit of whimsy and oddity are par for the course. I wouldn't do all this translation stuff if I didn't love me some wacky ole VTM. But basically, Melpominee as written isn't a power that I could see predators using on the <i>hunt</i>. Yeah, the same can be said of the several proprietary disciplines from the Big 13 -- looking at <i>you </i>Ravnos -- but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> So, my favored solution is thus: use the mechanics from <b>Mimetismo </b>from <b>Bloodlines: The Chosen</b>. It's a Nosferatu power, yes, but it fits really well with the Daughters. It has much more utility, too. I don't have my copy of <b>Chosen </b>on hand, but I might write up a second edition conversion when I get a chance, or at least expand on what the power ought to do in this context.<br /> <br /> If you're more interested in a flavour translation rather than a literal one, you could also just give them <b>Nightmare</b>. It can produce aural psychological illusions, albeit ones based around fear.<br /> <br /> <b>Kiasyd</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Weirdlings, Moths<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Mytherceria, plus two disciplines from the sire's clan<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Changeling Curse): </b>Kiasyd are burdened with the mercurial blood of the fae. When a Kiasyd reaches Humanity 6, she gains a single Bane not tied to Humanity, a ban or anathema reflecting the compulsive behaviors of the fair folk (see p. 108 of <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> for examples). This bane counts against the three banes a vampire is allowed, so Kiasyd are less able to mitigate detachment: coming from two supernatural worlds, their connection to humanity is flimsy. In addition, weapons forged from iron always do lethal damage to Weirdlings, even blunt weapons.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Intelligence or Wits<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> <br /> I went with the <b>V20 Dark Ages</b> version of the Kiasyd rather than &quot;Lasombra Faeries&quot;, because David Hill and co. came up with a really cool, plot hook oriented take on fae vampires, and I prefer it. In NWoD terms, a Kiasyd could be what happens when one Embraces a Fetch, or perhaps an enscorcelled mortal. Or a changeling...<br /> <br /> If you prefer the Lasombra bloodline version, then use their discipline spread as presented in <b>V20 </b>(though if you <i>really </i>want to go nuts, use their spread from Second Edition).<br /> <br /> As you can see, this Bane is similar to the Mekhet curse. I was going to write something up more closely reflecting their iron allergy, but I'm ultimately not a big fan of damage banes (Setites notwithstanding, but at least theirs enforces behaviour, to a degree). I also didn't want to go down the road of &quot;What is Cold Iron?&quot; I did end up leaving the iron weakness in on a smaller scale, because it fits with the flavor and the spirit of the Kiasyd, and being true to the source material has been important to my design aesthetic. But to me, modeling off the Mekhet curse fits because so much fae folklore revolves around them having odd bans and anathemas and the like (<b>Changeling </b>being a great example). That said, the minor banes presented in <b>Blood and Smoke</b> are more oriented to vampire legends, so you might want to come up with some custom banes that are more &quot;fae&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Mytherceria</b>...<br /> <br /> Like Melpominee, Mytherceria is a kitchen sink discipline. If I were building the Kiasyd from the ground up in NWoD -- as a bloodline, say -- I'd probably want to do Mytherceria as Blood Sorcery. Five tiers just doesn't encompass the number of things you could do with something that's supposed to reflect fae powers.<br /> <br /> Anyway, disclaimers aside, options:<br /> <br /> As with Melpominee, it wouldn't be difficult to directly translate the mechanics of the Classic version. For version, I (again) prefer <b>V20DA</b>. You can have a look at the raw manuscript via the Kickstarter page: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-v20-dark-ages\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...-v20-dark-ages</a><br /> <br /> If you want to use the mechanics of a published discipline, which riffs on an appropriate theme, <b>Sunnikuse </b>for the <b>Bohagande </b>in <b>Bloodlines: The Hidden </b>fits with the idea of fae as fate weavers and luck manipulators. It's not that similar to Mytherceria, but I don't think there really are any powers like that. I know Sunnikuse has a bad reputation for being &quot;broken&quot;, but I don't have any use for that term, and I think if you're going to have weird fae-pires in your game, you shouldn't be afraid to let your hair down. Do as thou wilt.<br /> <br /> Another appropriate theme you could play with is dreams. Contract of Dreams from first edition <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> is a good model, but it doesn't have the <i>oomph </i>that Kindred disciplines have, so a power boost might be in order.<br /> <br /> Taking Contracts as a model further, it might be interesting to just embrace Mytherceria's kitchen sink quality. Each tier of the Discipline could be a player-chosen clause from a <b>Changeling </b>Contract. That way, each Kiasyd is it's own unique creature, not quite Fae, but not quite a Vampire.<br /> <br /> That's it for now. I'll have more later, when I get home from work. As always, thoughts and suggestions are welcome. : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-14-2014, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T16:01:49-07:00","id":281568,"title":"","content":"I can't comment on the Sirens too much. I didn't ever use them as a player or ST in any of my cWoD games. No real interest in them, and they are one of the few ocWoD Bloodlines I feel are done justice with a Requiem-type Bloodline. Now, for the purposes of 13 Licks, I think what you've done is fair enough, and to keep it in line with the others, probably doing their Discipline as it's own is fair.<br /> <br /> Now the Kiasyd are more interesting. The Lasombra Fae are just one of many possibilities, with them opened up as a general Fae-touched vampire they have more to offer. Embraced Fetches, Changelings, Ensorcelled or half-fae are all possibilities, along with other, strange reasons to become Kiasyd (Thinkin' about how Marconius claimed to become Kiasyd), and in many ways they also resemble Requiem's base Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Now, Mythercia... I'm drawn to the hodgepodge 'take a Clause from a Contract!' approach, but from what we've seen Changeling 2e's Contracts will be wildly different, andn ot applicable. I think a port in the spirit of cWoD's Mythercia is a better option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T12:03:38-07:00","id":282567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=281568#post281568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the Kiasyd are more interesting. The Lasombra Fae are just one of many possibilities, with them opened up as a general Fae-touched vampire they have more to offer. Embraced Fetches, Changelings, Ensorcelled or half-fae are all possibilities, along with other, strange reasons to become Kiasyd (Thinkin' about how Marconius claimed to become Kiasyd), and in many ways they also resemble Requiem's base Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Kiasyd work really well as a Requiem-style bloodline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=281568#post281568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Mythercia... I'm drawn to the hodgepodge 'take a Clause from a Contract!' approach, but from what we've seen Changeling 2e's Contracts will be wildly different, andn ot applicable. I think a port in the spirit of cWoD's Mythercia is a better option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mytherceria is such a strange discipline conceptually. I'd just as soon say people should decide what translation works best on an individual basis. I favour Sunnikuse, but it needs some tweaking. I think my problem is that, as a player, I would love to make a Kiasyd character (specifically, the new Dark Ages version), but Mytherceria doesn't excite me at all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more bloodlines!<br /> <br /> <b>Baali</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Demons, Devils<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Daimonion, Majesty, Obfuscate<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Infernal Curse): </b>The Baali fear true faith. When faced with a religious symbol (a cross, a Star of David, the Takbir, etc.) wielded by a true believer, all of the Baali's dice pools are limited by her Humanity. A symbol held by a vampire has no effect. In addition, upon reaching Humanity 6, all Demons suffer the Plague of Purity bane (<b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, p. 108), which counts against the three banes a vampire is allowed.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Composure or Manipulation<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about the basic bane with this one. It has some teeth, but I'm not sure about the mechanics yet. I may grow to like it better as I think about it, but we'll see. I do like the extra Purity bane, though. My other idea for the main weakness is that when faced with a religious icon, even just a passive one (e.g., a church cross), they have to roll Humanity. If they fail, they gain Spooked or some custom Condition. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Daimoinon</b>/<b>Daimonion</b> (take your pick), I think it's actually pretty good as written, so I'll write up a quick translation when I get the chance. You could also give them Nightmare.<br /> <br /> <b>Samedi</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Stiffs, Zombies<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Obfuscate, Resilience, Thanatosis<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Putrid Curse): </b>Samedi rot as they fall to the Beast. All Physical dice pools are limited by the Stiff's Humanity. This does not apply to the passive bonus gained from Vigor or Resilience. In addition, Samedi are considered one Humanity dot lower than usual for the purposes of socializing with humans, as the smell of the grave follows them wherever they go.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Resolve or Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:<br /> <br /> Thanatosis </b>as written is neat conceptually, but a bit boring in terms of output. Mostly it's just a fancy way of wounding people and making them ugly. The turning to ashes stuff is cool, though. I'll see about translating it. I can't think of any published Requiem material that would make a good stand in, if that's your preference. You could just be done with it and say they have <b>Necromancy</b>, but in that case I'd replace Thanatosis with <b>Auspex</b>, and give them access to Necromancy for out of clan costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:18:14-07:00","id":282634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=282567#post282567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Kiasyd work really well as a Requiem-style bloodline.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mytherceria is such a strange discipline conceptually. I'd just as soon say people should decide what translation works best on an individual basis. I favour Sunnikuse, but it needs some tweaking. I think my problem is that, as a player, I would love to make a Kiasyd character (specifically, the new Dark Ages version), but Mytherceria doesn't excite me at all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more bloodlines!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. Perhaps we could come up with a more... unique take on Mytherceria. Because come CtL 2e, I don't think it'd be doable. Perhaps the Discipline can offer some of the Changeling's base traits in the Requiem system. Pledges, taking Vitae from Emotions, a mask effect, perhaps even have faux-Seemings and/or Kiths?<br /> <br /> Anyways, I love the DAV20 treatment of Daimonion, and would be thrilled to see it done. I have one request, you know the new Laibon bloodlines in DAV20? I think it'd be worthwhile to do those. Abombwe can even be the new Protean with some Devotions for it's Elder powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-15-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:25:39-07:00","id":282714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=282634#post282634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hrm. Perhaps we could come up with a more... unique take on Mytherceria. Because come CtL 2e, I don't think it'd be doable. Perhaps the Discipline can offer some of the Changeling's base traits in the Requiem system. Pledges, taking Vitae from Emotions, a mask effect, perhaps even have faux-Seemings and/or Kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. &quot;Changeling: The Discipline&quot;. Something involving Pledges and Talecrafting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T08:40:33-07:00","id":283883,"title":"","content":"You know, reading the DAV20 manuscript, I really want to convert the whole of it too the NWoD2.0 system. No relation too Requiem, just... all of it. Luckily, Yossarian's done most of the work. As it stands, you can use the physical discipline as VtR, plus the one's that already exist in both. I don't think I'd use Requiem-style Bloodlines at all, and just use cWoD style Clan/Bloodlines. Generation... that's a sticking point. I'm torn between using a Merit for Generation, or my old way where each Generation has a Minimum and Maximum Blood Potency. Maybe a Hybrid of both.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T23:41:47-07:00","id":284719,"title":"","content":"Is it alright if I pilfer all these house-rules for my own use? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T23:57:33-07:00","id":284724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=284719#post284719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it alright if I pilfer all these house-rules for my own use? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they're for! : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T12:24:30-07:00","id":285203,"title":"","content":"For those interested, I have a 2nd Edition compatible Merit to represent Generation. It doesn't replace the Blood Potency system, so those who want that kind of system, should enjoy it. This is based off some of Yossarian's ideas, my first iteration of Generation, and the various Generation-as-merit that have floated around since the Translation guide and before.<br /> <br /> <b>Generation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Special, Character Creation Only)</b><br /> Generation is Kindred's mystical bond with the first vampire -- its curse is strong, but so are its gifts. Supposedly, there are Thirteen Generations of Kindred from their progenitor. The Third Generation, the Antediluvians, were the progenitors of the Clans.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Unlike other Merits, Generation can only be acquired or increased through diablerie, but the diablerist gains nothing if her victim has fewer dots than her own Generation. After diablerie, the Merit automatically increases by one dot if the victim was of lower Generation than the diablerist. Childer usually gain one less dot in this Merit from their sires.<br /> <br /> Those that have this merit accrue Blood Potency faster than normal. If their rating in the Blood Potency trait is less than their rating in this merit they can purchase the next dot in Blood Potency by spending new 3 experience points (instead of the new 5 experience points as would be normal) and their Blood Potency will automatically increase by one dot every twenty five years until it is equal to their rating in this merit.<br /> <br /> In addition to this a vampire gains addition benefits from the list below. He acquires all the abilities in sequence. Those with Generation <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> gain the special abilities of the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd dot. Although this Merit decreases after Embrace, automatically lowering by one.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> For the first dot, you suffer under your Clan Bane at humanity seven. Additionally, your soul draws Diablerists to you. Auspex 2 can identify a Kindred's Generation.<br /> <br /> <b>0 (13th Generation)</b> Your Blood Potency starts out at one at the Embrace, and can only ever increase to five, and you have a greater chance to sire Revenants and Catiff's.<br /> <b>\u2022 (12th Generation)</b> You possess an <b>Iron Will</b>, once per story, the vampire may reflexively add double her dots in this Merit to any Resistance Attribute, or add it as a penalty to an opponent's own Resistance Attribute.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 (11th Generation)</b> You can spend one additional point of vitae each turn regardless of your normal Blood Potency determined allotment. Additionally, you apply a -1 to your Blood Potency for the purposes of determining whether you are restricted to human or vampire blood, +1 to your effective Blood Potency for purposes of Viniculum.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 (10th Generation)</b> You start the game with Blood Potency two and regardless of how long you spend in torpor your Blood Potency will never drop lower than two. If you acquire this rating in Generation through Diablerie and your Blood Potency was one before you performed that terrible act you first increase your Blood Potency to two and then, gain Experience from their Blood Potency. Additionally, you have a <b>Calloused Soul</b>, allowing you take take one extra Bane.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (9th Generation)</b> You add a further +1 to your Blood Potency for the purposes of determining the establishment of Vinculums . In addition, the smell of your vitae is especially enticing to addicts and its taste is even more compelling than a normal vampire\u2019s. Individuals that taste your vitae suffer a -1 penalty to their rolls to control vitae addiction and anyone who is currently addicted to vitae (suffering any penalties to those rolls due to previous tastes) who can smell your blood suffers a -1 penalty to their roll made to resist attempting to imbibe it.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (8th Generation)</b> You start the game with Blood Potency three and regardless of how long you spend in torpor your Blood Potency will never drop lower than three, and your maximum Blood Potency increases to six. If you acquire this rating in Generation through diablerie and your Blood Potency was one or two before you performed that terrible act you first increase your Blood Potency to three and then, if your victim had a Blood Potency higher than three, increase it by a further dot. In addition, you count your Blood Potency as 2 lower for purposes of feeding restrictions. Finally, you possess an <b>Apex Beast</b>, Vampires with Blood this potent may add dots in this Merit when Lashing out with Predatory Aura. In addition, vampires of higher Generations must spend a Willpower to fight back, regardless of Blood Potency.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 (7th Generation)</b> You start the game with Blood Potency three, your maximum Blood Potency is seven, and regardless of how long you spend in torpor your Blood Potency will never drop lower than three. If you acquire this rating in Generation through diablerie and your Blood Potency was one or two before you performed that terrible act you first increase your Blood Potency to three and then, if your victim had a Blood Potency higher than three, increase it by a further dot.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 (6th Generation) </b>You can spend two additional vitae (a total of three due to the 10th Generation benefit) each turn in addition to the allotment provided by your current Blood Potency, and your maximum Blood Potency is Eight. In addition you apply a -1 to your Blood Potency for the purposes of determining whether you are restricted to human or vampire blood (this stacks with the 11th Generation ability for a -2 total modifier for this purpose).<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 (5th Generation) </b>Your minimum Blood Potency is now four, and your maximum Blood Potency is nine. Those vampires Embraced into this Generation awoke from their deaths with a Blood Potency four and no matter how long they spend in torpor their rating in that trait never drops below four. If you acquire this rating in Generation through diablerie and your Blood Potency was three or less before you performed that terrible act you first increase your blood potency to four and then, if your victim had a Blood Potency higher than four, increase it by a further dot.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (4th Generation) </b>You add a further +1 to your Blood Potency for the purposes of determining the establishment of Vinculums, and your maximum Blood Potency is ten. In addition, the addictive qualities of your blood are heightened even further. Now, instead of the modifiers applied by 8th Generation blood, individuals that taste your vitae suffer a -2 penalty to their rolls to control vitae addiction and anyone who is currently addicted to vitae (suffering any penalties to those rolls due to previous tastes) who can smell your blood suffers a -2 penalty to their roll made to resist attempting to imbibe it. In addition, you add your current Blood Potency to the maximum amount of vitae you can have in your system at once. Lastly, Kindred with this potent blood have a <b>Methuselah's Mind </b>and are immune to the effects of a single mental or social discipline of her Clan (e.g., Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Obfuscate, etc.). These powers, or the effects of these powers, fail outright when used against her . If her clan has no appropriate Discipline, the player may choose one, though generally she should have dots in it. <b>Drawback: </b>This immunity does not apply if the discipline originated from a vampire with equal Generation. Also, the character's Blood Potency is considered two dots higher for the purposes of determining time spent in Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-19-2014, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T21:29:19-07:00","id":286371,"title":"","content":"So, my wife is wanting to play an Ahrimane for a DAV VtR game, so here's my little blurb for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahrimanes</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Valkyrie, Sister<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Vigor, Spiritus*<br /> <b>Bane - The Unbondable Curse:</b> The Ahrimane's blood resist's bondage, and in doing so, weaken's their ability to create Viniculum and ghouls. When the Ahrimane tries to create a ghoul, or use the blood bond, the subject first rolls 10 - Humanity dice to see if they automatically resist the Ahrimane's attempts.<br /> <b>Favorite Attribute:</b> Strength or Resolve<br /> *As it is, I'm using Blood Tenebrous (the 2nd Ed translation Falco did, up in the fan material thread) for Spiritus, since they do mostly the same thing, but BT is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 10-19-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:54:29-08:00","id":415844,"title":"","content":"This is rather nice, especially with the new Gangrel flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:43:52-08:00","id":416515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=286371#post286371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*As it is, I'm using Blood Tenebrous (the 2nd Ed translation Falco did, up in the fan material thread) for Spiritus, since they do mostly the same thing, but BT is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>link page please.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T15:09:28-07:00","id":433189,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, it's been a while!<br /> <br /> So, the Ravnos.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, I've never liked them. I've seen them played really well, but as a concept I don't have much love for them. Their power is bizarre and their weakness is a horrible stereotype. I don't actually think there's anything wrong with a clan of liars, <i>per se</i>, but with a clan that's supposed to be connected to Roma, it's ugly.<br /> <br /> So! I was thinking a lot about this after reading the preview of V20 Dark Ages that was posted on the open development blog, in that I really liked how they were recast in the light of being compulsive, whether to good or for ill, rather than being &quot;deceivers&quot;.<br /> <br /> In this light, I've changed up the Ravnos bane! Have a look!<br /> <br /> (I also reworded some stuff here and there, but nothing major.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:36:21-07:00","id":439678,"title":"","content":"Well I have to say this is one of the coolest things I've seen and downloaded it immediately. While I wont be running a game with it just yet(Planning on running a straight VtR game first), I think my next campaign will be using these. Although I have a few questions about the setting you use itself. Do kindred not lose their memories in torpor in your game? As they all know that they come from Caine. If so, how do they view Generation in light of the new Blood Potency system? Have you kept the Camirilla and Sabbat around, or do you use the new Covenants. Anyways, sorry to bombard you with questions, please respond to any of them at your leisure. Again, mad props for all the work you've put into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4902-letsgetspooky","name":"LetsGetSpooky","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:54:34-07:00","id":440221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LetsGetSpooky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=439678#post439678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have to say this is one of the coolest things I've seen and downloaded it immediately. While I wont be running a game with it just yet(Planning on running a straight VtR game first), I think my next campaign will be using these. Although I have a few questions about the setting you use itself. Do kindred not lose their memories in torpor in your game? As they all know that they come from Caine. If so, how do they view Generation in light of the new Blood Potency system? Have you kept the Camirilla and Sabbat around, or do you use the new Covenants. Anyways, sorry to bombard you with questions, please respond to any of them at your leisure. Again, mad props for all the work you've put into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always happy to answer questions!<br /> <br /> For torpor, the new edition of Vampire: The Requiem minimizes the Fog of Ages, so I just go with that. Vampires remember stuff. They might be sketchy memories, of course; human beings can barely remember last week, let alone 1000 years. But if Caine was your grandsire, you probably remember (if you believe him...!)<br /> <br /> When I've run this sort of mixed Masquiem game, I ax Generation as a power stat. I make it like Destiny in Mage, a Merit with which you can draw upon the strength of the First Vampire. Upthread, though, user Dreaminggod has a good hack for Generation based on something we talked about. But otherwise, I just use Blood Potency. Even when I run vanilla Masquerade, I prefer the idea that Generation is a lot less hard and fast than the Kindred like to pretend it is, and that the blood thickens <i>a little </i>on its own.<br /> <br /> As for the Cam and Sabbat, it depends. In the past, I've mixed the Sects and Covenants in a big stew, but that got tricky to keep straight. If I were running Masquerade with Requiem rules now, I'd probably just use the Masquerade setting, with some nods here and there to Requiem. That is, using their membership advantages, or maybe having the Covenants as minor cults and factions. Edit: Actually, I will say this -- whether or not I use them as a clan or a bloodline, I always make the Tremere into a Covenant. They <i>are </i>a Covenant in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If you haven't, you should check out the official<b> Vampire Translation Guide</b>. My work is (sort of) a patch of that for the second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-13-2015, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:49:59-07:00","id":446068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=440221#post440221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm always happy to answer questions!</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have one last question if you don't mind. I haven't bought the translation guide yet, although I doubt it covers this. How would you go about using Abominations in VtR. I know that OWoD has some stuff on their mechanics, but I'm not sure how they will translate into the new systems. In the game I am going to be starting, where 4 Invictus Dons who run the city are at war with a Garou Mob. I would like to introduce a small pack(3) of Abominations, but I'm not sure if they've considered this in the rules yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4902-letsgetspooky","name":"LetsGetSpooky","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:53:23-07:00","id":446085,"title":"","content":"They haven't.<br /> <br /> If I were gonna do it, I'd make it a product of the Strix using Synthesis or a similar power on one of the Uratha, and I'd probably have them equally hostile to both groups.<br /> <br /> But that'd depend on using 2e of Requiem and 2e of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:19:22-07:00","id":446120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=446085#post446085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They haven't.<br /> <br /> If I were gonna do it, I'd make it a product of the Strix using Synthesis or a similar power on one of the Uratha, and I'd probably have them equally hostile to both groups.<br /> <br /> But that'd depend on using 2e of Requiem and 2e of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do that too. That's really cool. Maybe give them some Strix dread powers?<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Translation Guide mostly just covers what's in the core Revised rulebook, and the first edition Requiem book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:10:11-07:00","id":446826,"title":"","content":"Still looking for falco's version of blood tenebrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T22:39:04-07:00","id":447167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=446826#post446826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still looking for falco's version of blood tenebrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! Didnt' see the earlier request, here you go; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nmvnt1UlBBR3DI6_Z1gFyqvPbSQtYi1pp6yIrcowHYM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...yIrcowHYM/edit</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:34:27-07:00","id":448285,"title":"","content":"If you're using 2e werewolf you could also have abominations be the handiwork of an idigam. <br /> <br /> &quot;alright, i'mma take a werewolf soul and stick it in a vampire, see what happens&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:33:34-07:00","id":455820,"title":"","content":"Wondering if you're going to cover the other Assamite castes, particularly the Vizers. I have problems with even a bloodline of honorable assassins, and would much rather present the Assamites by Vizers rather than Warriors, even if they are sort of a Malkavian/Toreador mix.<br /> <br /> I do plan to use these weaknesses though, running a Masquiem game at some point. However, I'll probably be removing the unique disciplines (Dementation becomes Nightmare, Obtenebration becomes Obfuscate, and Vicissitude and Serpent is become Protean, stuck on Chimerastry and Quietus right now) with a handful of clan-specific Devotions. I'll also change Caitiff to having no clan weakness but paying for all disciplines (even affinity coils) as out-of Clan disciplines, making them revenants without the suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:50:55-07:00","id":455824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=455820#post455820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wondering if you're going to cover the other Assamite castes, particularly the Vizers. I have problems with even a bloodline of honorable assassins, and would much rather present the Assamites by Vizers rather than Warriors, even if they are sort of a Malkavian/Toreador mix.<br /> <br /> I do plan to use these weaknesses though, running a Masquiem game at some point. However, I'll probably be removing the unique disciplines (Dementation becomes Nightmare, Obtenebration becomes Obfuscate, and Vicissitude and Serpent is become Protean, stuck on Chimerastry and Quietus right now) with a handful of clan-specific Devotions. I'll also change Caitiff to having no clan weakness but paying for all disciplines (even affinity coils) as out-of Clan disciplines, making them revenants without the suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dementation works to replace Chimerstry too - it has a couple of illusion-creating powers.<br /> <br /> For Assamites, make the tremere blood curse into the Assamite Clan weakness (treat kindred Vitae as a poison of Toxicity = [10 - Humanity]) and change the Clan Disciplines to Auspex, Obfuscate, and Vigor. Then the Sorcerer, Visier, and Warrior castes can be bloodlines that each add on that caste's weakness and all grant Quietus as the bloodline gift. Have quietus turn the character's blood into a poison with Toxicity equal to their Blood Potency. Then each caste can give a different set of Devotions that require Quietus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T10:01:56-07:00","id":455975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=455820#post455820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wondering if you're going to cover the other Assamite castes, particularly the Vizers. I have problems with even a bloodline of honorable assassins, and would much rather present the Assamites by Vizers rather than Warriors, even if they are sort of a Malkavian/Toreador mix.<br /> <br /> I do plan to use these weaknesses though, running a Masquiem game at some point. However, I'll probably be removing the unique disciplines (Dementation becomes Nightmare, Obtenebration becomes Obfuscate, and Vicissitude and Serpent is become Protean, stuck on Chimerastry and Quietus right now) with a handful of clan-specific Devotions. I'll also change Caitiff to having no clan weakness but paying for all disciplines (even affinity coils) as out-of Clan disciplines, making them revenants without the suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your thinking is pretty much exactly the same as mine about replacing the esoteric disciplines with common ones. I'm working (off and on) on a more complete patch for the Translation Guide, and that's one of the suggestions I make. For Quietus, I'd just give them Vigor. For Chimestry, I'd use Obfuscate, as it's much more able to do illusions now, though Nightmare could work too (it's a bit more Lost Boys).<br /> <br /> I'll see about getting to the other Assamites. If I find a slow moment at lunch, I might even post them today...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:55:44-07:00","id":456212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=455824#post455824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dementation works to replace Chimerstry too - it has a couple of illusion-creating powers.<br /> <br /> For Assamites, make the tremere blood curse into the Assamite Clan weakness (treat kindred Vitae as a poison of Toxicity = [10 - Humanity]) and change the Clan Disciplines to Auspex, Obfuscate, and Vigor. Then the Sorcerer, Visier, and Warrior castes can be bloodlines that each add on that caste's weakness and all grant Quietus as the bloodline gift. Have quietus turn the character's blood into a poison with Toxicity equal to their Blood Potency. Then each caste can give a different set of Devotions that require Quietus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, but I'd be more likely to go with Auspex, Celerity, and Obfuscate (seeing as those disciplines were in-clan for various Assamite castes in the cWoD). I'll see if I can come up with a version of Quietus for them, although I'm highly likely to limit it to the Warrior Caste (who'll likely swap out Auspex for Vigor) if I don't remove it entirely<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=455975#post455975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your thinking is pretty much exactly the same as mine about replacing the esoteric disciplines with common ones. I'm working (off and on) on a more complete patch for the Translation Guide, and that's one of the suggestions I make. For Quietus, I'd just give them Vigor. For Chimestry, I'd use Obfuscate, as it's much more able to do illusions now, though Nightmare could work too (it's a bit more Lost Boys).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, that you're updating the translation guide, I've looked through it and found it quite lacking myself (mainly the lack of anything outside the corebook, whereas I'm as likely to want Salubri and Cappadocians as Tremere and Giovanni). I'm actually just thinking of making the Tremere normal Tzimisce, As there isn't much need to legitimise them when the Antediluvians could just be a myth, and the Salubri interest me in their Dark Ages version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll see about getting to the other Assamites. If I find a slow moment at lunch, I might even post them today... </div> </div> </div>Cool, I'll be interested in seeing how they turn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:40:59-07:00","id":456230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456212#post456212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, but I'd be more likely to go with Auspex, Celerity, and Obfuscate (seeing as those disciplines were in-clan for various Assamite castes in the cWoD). I'll see if I can come up with a version of Quietus for them, although I'm highly likely to limit it to the Warrior Caste (who'll likely swap out Auspex for Vigor) if I don't remove it entirely</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity, that's what I meant to say, sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456212#post456212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, that you're updating the translation guide, I've looked through it and found it quite lacking myself (mainly the lack of anything outside the corebook, whereas I'm as likely to want Salubri and Cappadocians as Tremere and Giovanni). I'm actually just thinking of making the Tremere normal Tzimisce, As there isn't much need to legitimise them when the Antediluvians could just be a myth, and the Salubri interest me in their Dark Ages version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Tzimisce, what I do is give them Animalism since that's what Old Clan Tzimisci had, and made Vicissitude into a form of Blood Sorcery. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456212#post456212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, I'll be interested in seeing how they turn out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:17:20-07:00","id":456247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456230#post456230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Tzimisce, what I do is give them Animalism since that's what Old Clan Tzimisci had, and made Vicissitude into a form of Blood Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Old Clan Tzimisce had Animalism, Auspex and Dominate; with the normal clan having Animalism, Auspex, and Vicissitude. Vicissitude as a form of Blood Sorcery is interesting, but I think it works just as well as a series of Protean Devotions. The idea I have is to give the Tzimisce Animalism, Auspex, and Protean, and the Old Clan (if they exist) simply refuse to learn the Vicissitude devotions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:30:08-07:00","id":456261,"title":"","content":"Alright, here we go. Assamites all over the place!<br /> <br /> Caveat: A lot of ink has been spilled over the years over the Assamite castes. The Viziers and Sorcerers are often conflated, and for good reason. Personally, I'd simplify those distinctions in a Translation Guide game, and just merge the intellectual castes into a single Sorcerer caste, and just call them Viziers as a nickname. The Viziers always seemed superfluous to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite Viziers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Scholars, Artisans<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Celerity, Quietus<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Pedagogic Curse): </b>The Beasts of Viziers demand thoroughness in all things. Note the Scholar's highest Mental Skill. Whenever she gains an exceptional success using that Skill, including with disciplines, roll her Humanity. On failure, the Assamite gains the Persistent Obsession Condition in association with that Skill. For example, if the Skill were Academics, and the character were conducting research, she might become obsessed with finding every piece of information she can on the subject. If the character ever gains more dots in a different Mental Skill, the Obsession trigger shifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Composure or Intelligence<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Assamite Sorcerers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Magi, Witches<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, Quietus<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Mystic Curse): </b>Assamite sorcerers are beings bred of magic, and they cannot hide that. The Predatory Aura of a Magus is exceptionally obvious and occult. So blatant is her nature that whenever she engages in a Predatory Aura contest with a mortal, her dice pool is limited by her Humanity, as the opposition is easily able to size her up. If the mortal succeeds in contesting her, the Sorcerer gains the Condition she was attempting to impose. In addition, when attempting to track the character via indirect clues (<b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, p. 138) mortals do not subtract the character's dots in Obfuscate from their dice pools. This bane does not apply to interactions with other Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Intelligence or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>Assamite Sorcerers have access to the blood magic known as Dur-An-Ki.<br /> <br /> So, I kinda split the difference with the Sorcerers. They've had Auspex or Obfuscate depending on the edition, but because Requiem's paradigm doesn't tend to give out blood sorcery as clan disciplines, I've just given them both. I'm not sure if I like the Bane I came up with, but the Classic version is so weird and circumstantial, and it made sense to tie it into Predatory Aura.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-24-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:41:32-07:00","id":457370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456261#post456261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, here we go. Assamites all over the place!<br /> <br /> Caveat: A lot of ink has been spilled over the years over the Assamite castes. The Viziers and Sorcerers are often conflated, and for good reason. Personally, I'd simplify those distinctions in a Translation Guide game, and just merge the intellectual castes into a single Sorcerer caste, and just call them Viziers as a nickname. The Viziers always seemed superfluous to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite Viziers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Scholars, Artisans<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Celerity, Quietus<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Pedagogic Curse): </b>The Beasts of Viziers demand thoroughness in all things. Note the Scholar's highest Mental Skill. Whenever she gains an exceptional success using that Skill, including with disciplines, roll her Humanity. On failure, the Assamite gains the Persistent Obsession Condition in association with that Skill. For example, if the Skill were Academics, and the character were conducting research, she might become obsessed with finding every piece of information she can on the subject. If the character ever gains more dots in a different Mental Skill, the Obsession trigger shifts.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Composure or Intelligence<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Assamite Sorcerers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Magi, Witches<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, Quietus<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Mystic Curse): </b>Assamite sorcerers are beings bred of magic, and they cannot hide that. The Predatory Aura of a Magus is exceptionally obvious and occult. So blatant is her nature that whenever she engages in a Predatory Aura contest with a mortal, her dice pool is limited by her Humanity, as the opposition is easily able to size her up. If the mortal succeeds in contesting her, the Sorcerer gains the Condition she was attempting to impose. In addition, when attempting to track the character via indirect clues (<b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, p. 138) mortals do not subtract the character's dots in Obfuscate from their dice pools. This bane does not apply to interactions with other Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Intelligence or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>Assamite Sorcerers have access to the blood magic known as Dur-An-Ki.<br /> <br /> So, I kinda split the difference with the Sorcerers. They've had Auspex or Obfuscate depending on the edition, but because Requiem's paradigm doesn't tend to give out blood sorcery as clan disciplines, I've just given them both. I'm not sure if I like the Bane I came up with, but the Classic version is so weird and circumstantial, and it made sense to tie it into Predatory Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make them Mekhet. Quietus is achieved thru Duranki blood sorcery rituals on items.<br /> I might add the obsessive compulsive bane of the Dark Age Viziers for all.<br /> What distinguishes the castes is the focus of their skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:36:49-07:00","id":458256,"title":"","content":"Time for some deep cuts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nagaraja</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Serpent Kings, Flesh-Eaters<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Dominate, Protean<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Cannibal Curse): </b>The Beasts of Nagaraja are depraved and debased. In order to feed, the Serpent King must consume flesh along with blood. <span style=\"font-family:arial\">When feeding, s</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">he gains no nourishment from the first few Vitae taken, equal to 10 \u2013 Humanity</span></span>, unless she first eats a piece of her victim's flesh, inflicting two points of lethal damage. The Kiss of a Nagaraja always causes the Scarred Condition in mortals. This bane does not apply to feeding from other Kindred until Blood Potency 6.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Resolve or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>Members of Clan Nagaraja have access to Necromancy as an out-of-clan discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> The mechanics for the bane here seemed pretty obvious to me, especially in the sense that they don't make them utterly unplayable. Originally I thought I might make it so they had to inflict 10 - Humanity points of lethal damage, but that means that even at Humanity 6, they're killing almost every victim, and breaching the Masquerade like it's going out of style.<br /> <br /> I had a bit of trouble coming up with a third discipline, since if we're holding true to our pattern, Necromancy is out. I chose Protean because they have horrible serpent tooth-filled maws in cWoD, but I didn't want to pile onto their bane. Plus, I always wanted them to be able to do snake stuff, a la the Setites. If you don't like that particular twist on them, I'd give them Resilience instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>True Brujah</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Elois, Sages<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Majesty, Praestantia, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Clinical Curse): </b>Where the Brujah run hot, the True Brujah run cold. When interacting with others, treat the True Brujah's Humanity one dot lower than usual for determining Social penalties, and treat any Empathy failures as dramatic failures. This bane applies to all mortals, including Touchstones, <i>and </i>other vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Presence or Strength<br /> <br /> Not sure about this bane. It's modeled too much on Nosferatu, I think. I was tempted to just give them the new Ventrue bane, but that's not quite the archetype. A Ventrue feels like everyone around her is a pawn; a Trujah doesn't feel anything at all.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?<br /> <br /> Oh, and why not Temporis? Because <i>ehhhhhhhh</i>. It's complicated and tone breaking, even more so in <b>Requiem </b>than <b>Masquerade</b>. Plus, you could just rename Praestantia Temporis, if that suits you. PenDragon has a very good Second Edition conversion linked in the homebrew thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":".  Glitch in the Nagaraja bane 03-26-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T13:09:35-07:00","id":458288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=457370#post457370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make them Mekhet. Quietus is achieved thru Duranki blood sorcery rituals on items.<br /> I might add the obsessive compulsive bane of the Dark Age Viziers for all.<br /> What distinguishes the castes is the focus of their skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering using the Sorcerer bane and the Mekhet disciplines, and portray them as scholars of the unnatural (kinda like...the Mekhet), just because I don't like the genericness of the Mekhet bane (despite loving everything else about the Mekhet as shadowy scholars). But then again, I'm probably going to give the Ventrue refined tastes no matter which setting I run, and so might make Assamites and Mekhet different expressions of the same thing from different worlds (sort of like what I've done with the Brujah and Daeva, my Brujah are all about <i>intellectual passion</i> while my Daeva are about <i>social passion</i>), mainly because I plan to have Awakening mages accidentally link the two worlds together shortly after Gehenna, with the remnants of the Camarilla fleeing through the portal before it closes, and having them clash with the five requiem clans. I'll likely post a thread about it closer to the time I intend to run it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458256#post458256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time for some deep cuts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nagaraja</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Serpent Kings, Flesh-Eaters<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Dominate, Protean<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Cannibal Curse): </b>The Beasts of Nagaraja are depraved and debased. In order to feed, the Serpent King must consume flesh along with blood. Each time she feeds, a Nagaraja may only gain a number of Vitae equal to 10 - Humanity if she does not first eat a piece of her victim's flesh, inflicting two points of lethal damage. The Kiss of a Nagaraja always causes the Scarred Condition in mortals. This bane does not apply to feeding from other Kindred until Blood Potency 6.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Resolve or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>Members of Clan Nagaraja have access to Necromancy as an out-of-clan discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> The mechanics for the bane here seemed pretty obvious to me, especially in the sense that they don't make them utterly unplayable. Originally I thought I might make it so they had to inflict 10 - Humanity points of lethal damage, but that means that even at Humanity 6, they're killing almost every victim, and breaching the Masquerade like it's going out of style.<br /> <br /> I had a bit of trouble coming up with a third discipline, since if we're holding true to our pattern, Necromancy is out. I chose Protean because they have horrible serpent tooth-filled maws in cWoD, but I didn't want to pile onto their bane. Plus, I always wanted them to be able to do snake stuff, a la the Setites. If you don't like that particular twist on them, I'd give them Resilience instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like everything except for Protean, but I'm already highly tempted to update 2e Necromancy to Requiem anyway, it's a nice thematic set of ghost powers that I can see many vampires developing, and so it'll essentially be the 11th 'core' discipline, but not favoured by any clan. It would need a new name, but I'll probably use that in my personal games. The other problem is that the bane gets LESS restrictive as you lose humanity, at humanity 6 I can drain (10-6=)4 vitae from a person, whereas at Humanity 1 I can drain (10-1=)9 vitae without eating flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>True Brujah</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Elois, Sages<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Majesty, Praestantia, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Clinical Curse): </b>Where the Brujah run hot, the True Brujah run cold. When interacting with others, treat the True Brujah's Humanity one dot lower then usual for determining Social penalties, and treat any Empathy failures as dramatic failures. This bane applies to all mortals, including Touchstones, <i>and </i>other vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Presence or Strength<br /> <br /> Not sure about this bane. It's modeled too much on Nosferatu, I think. I was tempted to just give them the new Ventrue bane, but that's not quite the archetype. A Ventrue feels like everyone around her is a pawn; a Trujah doesn't feel anything at all.<br /> <br /> Suggestions?<br /> <br /> Oh, and why not Temporis? Because <i>ehhhhhhhh</i>. It's complicated and tone breaking, even more so in <b>Requiem </b>than <b>Masquerade</b>. Plus, you could just rename Praestantia Temporis, if that suits you. PenDragon has a very good Second Edition conversion linked in the homebrew thread. </div> </div> </div>I wish there was an official update of the Akhud for 2e, mainly because I really want to use the Praestantia discipline (the rest of it I've changed to make them walking masses of soul pieces, gaining more each time they feed) and don't own VII. I don't actually like Temporis, but then again apart from Necromancy I'm not particularly found of the 'mystical' disciplines, preferring for vampires to focus on the physical and psychic powers. I love the idea of Praestantia as their discipline, and think it works quite well for scholars.<br /> <br /> No ideas for the bane though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T13:29:30-07:00","id":458316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458288#post458288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like everything except for Protean, but I'm already highly tempted to update 2e Necromancy to Requiem anyway, it's a nice thematic set of ghost powers that I can see many vampires developing, and so it'll essentially be the 11th 'core' discipline, but not favoured by any clan. It would need a new name, but I'll probably use that in my personal games. The other problem is that the bane gets LESS restrictive as you lose humanity, at humanity 6 I can drain (10-6=)4 vitae from a person, whereas at Humanity 1 I can drain (10-1=)9 vitae without eating flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caught the glitch just before you posted; fixed!<br /> <br /> And yeah, Protean is more a whimsical choice on my part. Resilience (or Vigor?) is probably better. The reason I didn't give them Necromancy is because, as per the Translation Guide (and Requiem in general), blood sorcery doesn't work as an inherent quality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458288#post458288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish there was an official update of the Akhud for 2e, mainly because I really want to use the Praestantia discipline (the rest of it I've changed to make them walking masses of soul pieces, gaining more each time they feed) and don't own VII. I don't actually like Temporis, but then again apart from Necromancy I'm not particularly found of the 'mystical' disciplines, preferring for vampires to focus on the physical and psychic powers. I love the idea of Praestantia as their discipline, and think it works quite well for scholars.<br /> <br /> No ideas for the bane though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd also like to see an official update on Praestantia.<br /> <br /> From a certain perspective, Temporis could be a form of blood magic, but I think it's still a bit wacky for <b>Requiem</b>'s system and mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:02:52-07:00","id":458369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458316#post458316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caught the glitch just before you posted; fixed!<br /> <br /> And yeah, Protean is more a whimsical choice on my part. Resilience (or Vigor?) is probably better. The reason I didn't give them Necromancy is because, as per the Translation Guide (and Requiem in general), blood sorcery doesn't work as an inherent quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of Resilience, Vigor or Protean really fit the flavour. As I understand, the original Nagaraja were death mages, so why not give them Getsumei or Cattivera as their third discipline? It would be great for the Cappadocians and Samedi as well, a relatively balanced necromancer power for the death bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I am going to update the old Necromancy discipline from 1e/2e (the non-blood magic one), just because it feels like something that one vampire or another would develop. But that's for another thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I'd also like to see an official update on Praestantia.<br /> <br /> From a certain perspective, Temporis could be a form of blood magic, but I think it's still a bit wacky for <b>Requiem</b>'s system and mood. </div> </div> </div>I currently refuse to use the 2e homebrew version out of principle, but I'm considering giving the Akhud Auspex/Celerity/Vigor until I have access to either a 1e or 2e official version legally, and then Auspex/Celerity/Praestantia. The version I'm using is not 'quiet' enough for obfuscate, but again, off topic.<br /> <br /> I could see a handful of Temporis powers as celerity components, but I agree that most masquerade blood magic/mystical disciplines are too wacky and actually detracts from the Gothic Punk aspect slightly. I'd actually be glad if no time-control powers appear in Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:21:44-07:00","id":458396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458369#post458369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think any of Resilience, Vigor or Protean really fit the flavour. As I understand, the original Nagaraja were death mages, so why not give them Getsumei or Cattivera as their third discipline? It would be great for the Cappadocians and Samedi as well, a relatively balanced necromancer power for the death bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I am going to update the old Necromancy discipline from 1e/2e (the non-blood magic one), just because it feels like something that one vampire or another would develop. But that's for another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm definitely in favour of letting them have access to Necromancy, I just wouldn't bake it into their template.<br /> <br /> As for third discipline, it's ultimately pretty subjective because they're such a niche clan, but I could definitely see them with one of the necromantic flavoured bloodline disciplines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458369#post458369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I currently refuse to use the 2e homebrew version out of principle, but I'm considering giving the Akhud Auspex/Celerity/Vigor until I have access to either a 1e or 2e official version legally, and then Auspex/Celerity/Praestantia. The version I'm using is not 'quiet' enough for obfuscate, but again, off topic.<br /> <br /> I could see a handful of Temporis powers as celerity components, but I agree that most masquerade blood magic/mystical disciplines are too wacky and actually detracts from the Gothic Punk aspect slightly. I'd actually be glad if no time-control powers appear in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, maybe Temporis could be something for the Holy Engineers...even then, though, it's a bit off the beaten path. And I'm not that interested in converting it, ultimately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:51:36-07:00","id":458410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=458396#post458396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm definitely in favour of letting them have access to Necromancy, I just wouldn't bake it into their template.<br /> <br /> As for third discipline, it's ultimately pretty subjective because they're such a niche clan, but I could definitely see them with one of the necromantic flavoured bloodline disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what we need to decide is 'do they need a physical discipline, and if so, which of their three disciplines is least central to their concept', and I'd say that if we do want to give them one (Celerity, Protean, Resilience, or Vigor) then Dominate is the discipline that should be replaced, but I don't really care, their the one I'm least likely to use, I'd rather just have a surviving branch of the Cappadocians who have become vengeful (possibly the Harbingers of Skulls, possibly not, depending on the game) filling the creepy death mage niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, maybe Temporis could be something for the Holy Engineers...even then, though, it's a bit off the beaten path. And I'm not that interested in converting it, ultimately. </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't think it's worth the effort to make it balanced myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 03-26-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T18:55:47-07:00","id":476492,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I really like the Gangrel bane, especially in comparison to the oWoD version, which was a little OTT since, over time, it basically turned you into a walking monstrous Chimera to beat a Nosferatu in terms of social penalties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I might actually see about using it in my own games as an alternative to the Feral Curse, or perhaps apply it to an especially beastly bloodline of the Gangrel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:20:33-07:00","id":476766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=476492#post476492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I really like the Gangrel bane, especially in comparison to the oWoD version, which was a little OTT since, over time, it basically turned you into a walking monstrous Chimera to beat a Nosferatu in terms of social penalties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I might actually see about using it in my own games as an alternative to the Feral Curse, or perhaps apply it to an especially beastly bloodline of the Gangrel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! The Gangrel Bane took a long time to work the kinks out of.<br /> <br /> All of these banes could work in a vanilla Requiem game, I think, as either Humanity banes or weaknesses for bloodlines (though bloodline banes don't have to scale with Humanity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":".  The Autocorrect Curse 04-11-2015, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:50:02-07:00","id":478333,"title":"","content":"Small update!<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador: </b>Being Engrossed now upgrades failures on Social actions to dramatic failures, rather than removing 10-again.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere: </b>As much as I liked the bane as it was, I realised it didn't scale with Humanity (i.e., it didn't get worse as your Humanity fell). This is the new text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>13 Licks</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Yielding Curse):</b> Tremere are more vulnerable to Vinculums. A Warlock will form a second step blood bond to a vampire the first time she drinks from him, and treats her Touchstones as attaching one dot higher than usual on detachment rolls incurred for harming her regnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering making that two dots higher, but that might be too much.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:13:52-07:00","id":478345,"title":"","content":"@Yossariaon:<br /> <br /> Have you considered giving them special Conditions added to the Blood Bond instead? These Conditions could then be resisted with Humanity rolls, lik the Daeva curse. They do not bond faster, but <b>harder</b>. This would also give players an incentive to actually subjecting themselves to their Clan Bane, when otherwise it would be fairly easy to ignore (depending on how exactly you run the Tremere in a Masquiem game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 04-12-2015, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:04:28-07:00","id":481313,"title":"","content":"I've already headcannoned that in my WoD Caine was a Beast who killed his brother in his Homecoming, and eventually developed into a vampire, learning how to Embrace others into the Family. So we get the familial clans. Of course, he's not the only vampire either. Just where a good portion of vampires come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:01:32-07:00","id":485468,"title":"","content":"Will the Bloodline conversions be added to the .PDF file?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T15:09:48-07:00","id":485771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=485468#post485468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Bloodline conversions be added to the .PDF file?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've considered doing a separate PDF with just the bloodlines. The only thing is, to be truly complete, I'd have to convert some of their disciplines, which is more involved than coming up with Banes, and I have less of a template to go off because the Translation Guide only included powers and clans from Revised Vampire. It comes down to how interested I am in doing it, and how much spare time I want to dedicate to it.<br /> <br /> So long story short, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:36:30-07:00","id":486188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=285203#post285203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Generation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Special, Character Creation Only)</b><br /> Generation is Kindred's mystical bond with the first vampire -- its curse is strong, but so are its gifts. Supposedly, there are Thirteen Generations of Kindred from their progenitor. The Third Generation, the Antediluvians, were the progenitors of the Clans.<br /> <br /> ...(awesome stuff)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoutout for awesomeness for this! This is exactly what I need to incorporate Generation into my Masquiem game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:15:04-07:00","id":600825,"title":"","content":"Bored at work? Nothing to do at work? Obscure bloodlines time.<br /> <br /> As usual, my baseline is V20 Dark Ages. It's available as raw text on its Kickstarter page, and for purchase fairly soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Anda</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Tartars, Wanderers<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Protean, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Exile Curse): </b>The Anda Beast craves community with its people as much as it does blood. All Tartars must have at least one Touchstone who is also a blood relative (though this can be a fairly distant relation, within reason). If the Anda spends a number of nights equal to Humanity away from a blood-related Touchstone, she gains the Lethargic Condition, and cannot resolve it until she has a significant interaction with him again, even after taking a full day of rest.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Composure or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b><br /> <br /> In <b>V20DA</b> these guys pretty much already have a <b>Requiem </b>style bane. I won't reprint it here, but if you prefer, you could use that exactly as written. For 13 Licks (I guess that what we're calling this now?), I changed it up because Touchstones are underused in my conversions, and I wanted to do something other than copy pasting. So I'm sort of breaking my rule about trying to stay as close as possible to the original, because you don't really need me to convert the original. This bane is my interpretation of the Anda's schtick: that is, keeping ties to the mortals they ride with out on the steppes, even as they're permanently separated from the bulk of their people. It probably doesn't work as well in a modern setting, all things considered, but I think it fits with the nomadic style of Mongol armies in a Dark Ages setting.<br /> <br /> I considered switching Composure with Strength for their Favored Attributes, but the Anda are fairly close to the Gangrel baseline, archetypally.<br /> <br /> <b>Lamiae</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Gorgons, Lilins<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Auspex , Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Infectious Curse): </b>The Lamiae bite is excruciating, and potentially virulent. Gorgons have no Kiss effect, and can only inflict the Scarred Condition on their vessels. In addition, Lamiae carry the Seed of Lilith, a horrible, leprous disease their victims sometimes contract. Each time a Lamiae feeds, the vessel must roll Stamina + Resolve to avoid contracting it. On failure, the victim is infected by a poison with a Toxicity rating equal to 10 minus the Lamia's Humanity. The victim takes damage once a night until he fully resists it, or dies. Lamiae may feed from other Kindred normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Strength or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Special: </b>Lamiae have access to Necromancy as an out-of-clan discipline.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b><br /> <br /> Took a little note from the Giovanni bane, but this is more or less what the original does. The only thing missing is their Path of Necromancy, but Necromancy needs to be updated to 2nd Edition rules first.<br /> <br /> Edit: Because it was a pain to trawl through this thread to find them, the bloodlines are all now listed in the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 07-23-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T16:27:35-07:00","id":601032,"title":"","content":"You forgot the Salubri (All three Castes?) in the Bloodlines page. <br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Healers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Unicorns, Soulsuckers (derogatory) <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Majesty, Valeren (Obeah?)<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Gentle Curse): </b>Salubri Healers take 10 - Humanity less vitae from vessels who are not willing. Those enthralled by Majesty count as willing targets.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Intelligence or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Warriors</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Cyclopses, Kin-Slayers<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Resilience, Valeren<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Dominance Curse): </b>Salubri Warriors must test their strength and establish martial dominance; they take 10 - Road less vitae from their victim if they don't establish dominance. This may be defined as a duel to the death, or a simple brawl to Incapacitated. A few Warrior Herds comprise of companions who\u2019ve been beaten down in the training yard.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Strength or Wits<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Watchers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>--<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, Valeren<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Obsessive Curse): </b>Watchers can be remarkably short-sighted, having a tendency to fixate on their preferred small details and ignore the larger conceptual picture. Watchers must choose a field of study narrow enough for a Knowledge specialty, such as the Ten Thousand Demons, a specific mortal culture or the esoterics of Necromancy. Watchers must succeed on a Humanity roll to pass up an opportunity (as defined by the Storyteller) to acquire or study knowledge of their field, or lose two dice from all pools for the remainder of the night.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Dexterity or Intelligence<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of DAV20, thought about doing the African bloodlines from there? They fit VtR really well (And VtM, obviously) and are excellent to boot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T16:52:12-07:00","id":601058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=601032#post601032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot the Salubri (All three Castes?) in the Bloodlines page.<br /> ...<br /> Also, speaking of DAV20, thought about doing the African bloodlines from there? They fit VtR really well (And VtM, obviously) and are excellent to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite right, I did forget! They were probably in my old updates, but I'd rather start fresh. I'll probably tool around with those on my own, though I like what you came up with.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'll definitely get around to the African bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:52:58-07:00","id":602281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=456230#post456230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of Tzimisce, what I do is give them Animalism since that's what Old Clan Tzimisci had, and made Vicissitude into a form of Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Me too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you are using the dynamic blood sorcery I'd make transformation a favored theme.<br /> Despite the Flavour text saying that Koldunic is very efficient in its blood use(suggesting theban) , I see it as very bloody therefore more cruac like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T00:27:01-07:00","id":602687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=601032#post601032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot the Salubri (All three Castes?) in the Bloodlines page. <br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Healers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Unicorns, Soulsuckers (derogatory) <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Majesty, Valeren (Obeah?)<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Gentle Curse): </b>Salubri Healers take 10 - Humanity less vitae from vessels who are not willing. Those enthralled by Majesty count as willing targets.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Intelligence or Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Warriors</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Cyclopses, Kin-Slayers<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Resilience, Valeren<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Dominance Curse): </b>Salubri Warriors must test their strength and establish martial dominance; they take 10 - Road less vitae from their victim if they don't establish dominance. This may be defined as a duel to the death, or a simple brawl to Incapacitated. A few Warrior Herds comprise of companions who\u2019ve been beaten down in the training yard.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Strength or Wits<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri Watchers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>--<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, Valeren<br /> <b>Clan Bane (The Obsessive Curse): </b>Watchers can be remarkably short-sighted, having a tendency to fixate on their preferred small details and ignore the larger conceptual picture. Watchers must choose a field of study narrow enough for a Knowledge specialty, such as the Ten Thousand Demons, a specific mortal culture or the esoterics of Necromancy. Watchers must succeed on a Humanity roll to pass up an opportunity (as defined by the Storyteller) to acquire or study knowledge of their field, or lose two dice from all pools for the remainder of the night.<br /> <b>Favored Attributes: </b>Dexterity or Intelligence<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of DAV20, thought about doing the African bloodlines from there? They fit VtR really well (And VtM, obviously) and are excellent to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give healers back their Resilience/Fortitude.<br /> <br /> And what's a Watcher Salubri, there are only two castes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:44:22-07:00","id":603798,"title":"","content":"Nooo.... I like the DAV20 Salubri, they are the most fleshed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:40:08-07:00","id":603937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=603798#post603798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nooo.... I like the DAV20 Salubri, they are the most fleshed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get why a third caste was needed, I like the healer/warrior dynamic and have it as a more passive/active version. I also believe that the ONLY difference between the castes should be the path of Valaren that they learn, and that you can do a lot by just presenting the Salubri clan/bloodline and saying that a Salubri can only learn one of the X paths of Valeran (so yes you can have your Watchers, but they don't get a different discipline or curse), but then I'd recommend bringing the powers into something closer to variations on the same theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T15:43:59-07:00","id":604276,"title":"","content":"I never understood why some Clans had these castes. Is it because the clan in question is supposed to be a big faction, and different castes allow different types of characters within an Assamite/Salubri game?<br /> <br /> Or does it have to do with a way Bloodlines work in the context of Masquerade? If so, should it actually be modeled by a different Clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T19:01:23-07:00","id":604389,"title":"","content":"It's based VtM's Bloodlines. They are splinters from the main clan, so the 'castes' are a bunch of closely related Bloodlines all descended from the same Antediluvian. Masquerade modeled all their Bloodlines like clans. So, I model my Masquiem Clans and Bloodlines the same ways, especially since Requiem 2.0 models Bloodlines SO differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T20:58:20-07:00","id":604453,"title":"","content":"Makes sense I guess. In the absence of Banes it's not a bad way to get a diverse bunch of curses for the different bloodlines. It would've been cool if they gave them a bit more distinctly interesting identity at least in the names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T22:18:12-07:00","id":604496,"title":"","content":"Well, Bloodlines that developed in ways that arn't part of a structure (so, basically, bloodlines of anyone but the Salubri and Assamite mainly) have more... inspired names. Everyone treats them as a member of the same Clan. Where as, say, the Danava (a Indian bloodline of the Ventrue) who are way off from the main clan, and are much more different than main Bloodline. Then there are ones like the Niktuku who may actually be the parent clan, and not the Nosferatu. <br /> <br /> In many ways, with Bloodlines being structured and mechanically like clans, it makes it harder to tell who came first. <br /> <br /> However, Clans that include Bloodlines under their clan structure treat all 'bloodlines' as full members and all as one clan. In VtM Clans are both bloodlines, families and social structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:05:00-07:00","id":604954,"title":"","content":"I've always liked the castes (in general). They add a level of weirdness to the Masquerade clan structure, and a better sense of why clans are both families and political factions. I'd actually like it if every clan had some sort of caste system. But then, I love bloodlines, both for Masquerade and Requiem, so it might have something to do with that.<br /> <br /> I'll see about doing a take on the Salubri tonight, though I suspect it's going to look a lot like what Dreaminggod came up with. I do have an idea about defining the castes a little differently though...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T20:52:15-07:00","id":607465,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks! I'm still curious to see your Salubri (I also need to convert Watcher Valeren), I like your work, and your Banes will probably be better than mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T11:27:31-07:00","id":682242,"title":"","content":"If anyone is interested, I've begun to compile a more complete conversion of VtM. I'm slowly translating the Disciplines to a 5-dot with Devotions for Elder powers format. The clans are courtesy of Yossarian (barring some changes I've made). I'll be honest it's being written for my hosue world, so you'll notice some changes (The Black Hand covenant absorbed the other bits of Sabbat plus the False and True Black Hand that were worth keeping, and not taken by others Covenants. Minus the Belial's Brood, who I'm going to make a Baali run Covenant of pure Infernalists.) that may be rather specific to my brand of mash-up between the two.It, otherwise, barrows more from Masquerade than Requiem. As a note, any template changes not listed are the same as Requiem's Kindred (Kindred Senses, et al) and the more excellent rendition of the other Disicplines use VtR 2e's versions. My only house rule (that is not put in yet) is Auspex 2 has Aura Perception, using a modified version of the psychic merit. I've not added it there yet because I'm not sure which I'm using.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, people can take apart, use or critique what they want. The link is in my sig. If anything else from my folder of things goes uncredited to their original maker, send me a PM and I'll add that it was originally yours. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 09-29-2015, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:24:28-07:00","id":682426,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this the other day when Eddy posted his blog about making Humanity relevant again in V4. Converting the clan weaknesses to using Humanity as a reference stat would go a long way to fixing the problem, in my opinion. I would have commented on it, but I feel that the old V:tM system is so fundamentally broken, that fixing it would basically be just reskinning Requiem. A testament to how good Requiem is, in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:07:49-07:00","id":683131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=682426#post682426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about this the other day when Eddy posted his blog about making Humanity relevant again in V4. Converting the clan weaknesses to using Humanity as a reference stat would go a long way to fixing the problem, in my opinion. I would have commented on it, but I feel that the old V:tM system is so fundamentally broken, that fixing it would basically be just reskinning Requiem. A testament to how good Requiem is, in my view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested to see how V4 differentiates itself from both Revised/V20 <i>and </i>Requiem, though it certainly wouldn't hurt to take a few cues from the younger sibling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:36:06-07:00","id":683607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=683131#post683131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested to see how V4 differentiates itself from both Revised/V20 <i>and </i>Requiem, though it certainly wouldn't hurt to take a few cues from the younger sibling.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I desperately hope they get rid of is the other paths besides humanity. Without going into too much of a tangent in this thread, using a path completely circumvents the threat of humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:51:49-07:00","id":683618,"title":"","content":"I think that's the general idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:13:50-07:00","id":683627,"title":"","content":"I phrased that poorly. What I meant to say was that when you can select what your degeneration triggers are, you can eliminate the points what would normally cause a rating loss. Essentially, the Path of What I Was Going to Do Anyways. A path that says helping an helpless old grandmother across the street is bad, while straight-up murdering her is okay is essentially a useless tool for roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T00:04:41-07:00","id":684001,"title":"","content":"Is it though? What if you encounter a situation where helping a helpless old grandmother is a tactically sound decision? <br /> <br /> Like maybe she has access to some rare artifact, and you're trying to ingratiate yourself with her in order to get it. Suddenly, you have to be nice to this person, which totally goes against your principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:40:02-07:00","id":684090,"title":"","content":"Also, while I'm showing my things, have my small 'conversion' for the Wan Kuei for NWoD, more based off of the Wicked Dead material. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14hmFIwjxtsrE_ko4G8hT7zjV9Av3Fg4D0zt-C7pemXY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t-C7pemXY/edit</a> <br /> <br /> Gui Ren, the Hungry Dead. <br /> <br /> I was, once upon a time, going to run a game in LA, and wanted to include the other, non-Cainite, asian vampires. Not happy with most of KotE (but liking enough to want to salvage it) this was my best way to do it, for the least amount of work.<br /> <br /> I never worked on their Dharmas and since they were all written as NPCs eye-balled the Dharmas from the book (The Dharma's took the place of Covenants, and Humanity all at once) so that isn't included. All in all, they are Clanless vampires with their Blood Potency tied to the Dharmas. They use Kindred Disciplines, and have different rules for waking up. (That's when their Chi balance is Chosen. I didn't include Balanced chi balance though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:43:01-07:00","id":685127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke?p=684001#post684001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it though? What if you encounter a situation where helping a helpless old grandmother is a tactically sound decision?<br /> <br /> Like maybe she has access to some rare artifact, and you're trying to ingratiate yourself with her in order to get it. Suddenly, you have to be nice to this person, which totally goes against your principles.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess the issue I have with paths is that they are supposed to be a way that a Kindred deals with her nature in order to stave off the Beast. If a Kindred reaches Humanity 0 - Must sleep. Must feed. Must kill. How does a path that encourages killing, or any behavior that invites the Beast to the forefront over the Man, actually prevent the Beast from taking over eventually? Shouldn't an action that any humane person would do (helping the grandmother) reinforce Humanity, rather than ruin it? I know the whole tagline is &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become,&quot; but ever since the Humanity revamp (heh) in 2nd edition Requiem, I can't see it any other way. One can either act like a human, which entails all the good and most of the bad behavior covered in the paths, or one can act like the Beast and lose everything to it.<br /> <br /> I will most likely pick up V4, but I doubt I'll ever play it. Requiem scratches all of my itches. I'll stop derailing Yossarian's thread now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T22:40:26-07:00","id":687953,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[SIDEBAR]</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Bloodline, Clan or Caste?</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">What is the differences and separations of Clans, Bloodlines and Castes? Unlike </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Vampire: the Requiem</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> the Kindred do not join Bloodlines (most of them anyways, some are eligible to be joined), but are Embraced into them. Like Requiem a Bloodline split off from a Clan and changed the Blood, however, in many ways, they act as a separate Clan. Castes on the other hand, all read as a member of their \u2018Clan\u2019.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The major deciding factor in what is a Clan, Bloodline or a Caste of the Clan is status, and Blood Sympathy. What differentiates a Bloodline from a Caste is every Caste shares Blood Sympathy with the others; Assamite Warriors, Sorcerers and Viziers each have Blood Sympathy, whereas an Anda and a Gangrel do not share Blood Sympathy, while being closer in Discipline spread, the Blood of an Anda does not read as that of a Gangrel. However, Grecian Gangrel and a Country Gangrel all share a Clan-level Blood Sympathy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">What makes a Bloodline a bloodline and not a Clan is status, and lineage. Vampires who share the Curses of Caine and control much power, along with having a lineage that stretches back to the earliest nights qualifies one as a Clan. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[/SIDEBAR]<br /> <br /> Alright, this is my personal interpretation for what makes a Clan, Bloodline or Caste in my Masquiem game.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:48:18-08:00","id":1058731,"title":"","content":"Suuuuuper Thread Necromancy!<br /> <br /> In a fit of pique, I changed some things:<br /> <br /> <b>Setites:</b> The bright light effect was adjusted. It was a little too harsh, and the sunlight bane is more where their (in)humanity comes into play.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra: </b>What I had before (i.e., mortals find it easier to recognize your reflection, or lack thereof) was boring, so I made it significantly more like, but not quite, the Hollow Mekhet curse. This is definitely further from what the VtM weakness was, but, like the Tzimisce, I'm on record as finding the Lasombra weakness flavorful but not very interesting in practice.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian: </b>This one never quite sat right with me; it reused a published Condition, and it didn't operate like any other bane. I also reflavoured it to be less that Malkavians are mentally ill, and more that they (maybe) see the world like changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Appendix:</b> Adjusted some of the Conditions<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:46:30-08:00","id":1060075,"title":"","content":"edit: Never mind, can't read.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}